Package: salami-device
Version: 0.42
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: OnePlus 11 mainline port <noreply@localhost>
Depends: systemd, systemd-zram-generator, systemd-oomd, irqbalance, rtkit, mobile-broadband-provider-info, openssh-server, python3, rmtfs (>= 1.1.1-2+salami1), zstd, linux-firmware-qualcomm-wireless, wireless-regdb, linux-firmware-qualcomm-graphics, usb-modeswitch, bluez, dmsetup, iw
Recommends: python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: OnePlus 11 (salami) device integration
 USB NCM gadget with a DHCP lease for the directly attached host, an
 optional unauthenticated root shell on that link for bring-up, SSH
 key-only login, first-boot SSH host key generation, and marking the
 boot slot successful in the GPT after boot. Graphical sessions preload a
 small library that keeps llvmpipe's JIT off SVE, which the firmware disables.
 The phone's own ADSP/CDSP/modem firmware and modem EFS are copied from its
 partitions on first boot; rmtfs serves the EFS copies, so the modem never
 writes the partitions. Wi-Fi uses the Qualcomm reference board data
 from linux-firmware under this board's name and a stable per-machine MAC.
 Active remote administrators can scan Wi-Fi and manage network connections.
 With the matching battery driver, charging defaults to an 80 percent ceiling,
 and the original charger may run SUPERVOOC fast charging.
 USB modem mode switching supports the tested Huawei CDC Ethernet adapter.
 The GPU and Iris3 video codec use this phone's signed firmware, imported from
 read-only vendor_a, and GNOME Remote Desktop can access the hardware render node.
 Remote-login sessions keep their virtual display active while physical
 screen blanking remains independent.
 Sound uses an AudioReach topology and UCM profile for the two speakers
 and two microphones.
 Android boot, firmware and calibration partitions remain available to system
 services but are hidden from desktop volume lists and automatic mounting.
 Remote administrators can switch radios via /dev/rfkill, and APT periodic
 timers check NetworkManager online status instead of timing out on networkd.
 Power button short presses toggle screen blanking and long presses prompt to
 shut down. A GNOME Shell extension guards modal dialogs against an upstream
 on-screen-keyboard null-actor exception, prevents GDM user-list overlap,
 keeps the GDM login dialog visible across idle blanking and wake, guards
 cellular indicator initialization, supports optional remote-greeter
 auto-login, and provides both a top-bar AppIndicator control center
 (salami-tray: live battery/power/temp pill plus point-and-click perf, charge
 ceiling, physical screen DPMS/brightness, torch, refresh rate, RDP quality,
 and server maintenance) and Quick Settings toggles. Includes salami-ctl CLI,
 irqbalance multi-core IRQ distribution, UFS 4.0 queue tuning, Wi-Fi
 low-latency power-save override, automatic Wi-Fi/5G WAN failover, PSI
 early-OOM protection, 8 MiB QUIC/SMB/RDP socket buffers with BBR + FQ + PMTU
 probing, cellular QMAP MTU 1496, and a 512 MiB journal cap.
